# The Docker build context is an allowlist: only what `next build` needs. Anything not named here stays out,
# so a new file (a secret, a dump, a screenshot) never reaches an image by accident.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!next.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!src/
!public/
!scripts/healthcheck.mjs

# Never in the image, even inside an allowed folder: settings and secrets (.env.example is not needed either),
# dependencies and build output (the Dockerfile makes its own), tests and their output.
**/.env*
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
**/shots
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
